      "caption": "Supplemental available-case natural accuracy and measured cost for all seventeen procedures. Accuracy averages A-seasonal-scaled MSE equally over series within each available collection, then equally over the three available collections (seven series). The horizontal coordinate is the arithmetic mean measured procedure time across those seven available tasks, with equal task weights and a logarithmic axis. Thus accuracy and time use explicitly different weighting rules. Time includes the implementation's charged fitting, selection and eager query dependencies and selected-state packing/serialization on this host; candidate dependencies are counted once for the non-KAHM policy. Downloads, process imports, data preparation and artifact writes are excluded. Numbered points identify all procedures; overlapping points share the same plotted coordinates. There are no uncertainty intervals or source-population claims. The planned four-collection aggregate remains undefined because the three frozen rideshare tasks were unavailable; this figure does not replace it.",
